  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>How many of the following metal ions have similar value of spin only magnetic moment in gaseous state? ________</p><p>(Given: Atomic number<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cr</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Ni</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From magnetic moment formula:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mi>BM</mi><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math> no. of unpaired electrons )</p><p>Ion&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;E.C.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; n<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#38;</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;have same value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></math></p>",
